  "term": "binocular fusion",
  "definition": "Binocular fusion is the combining by the two eyes of separate but corresponding images into one visual experience, often yielding a single impression of depth or solidity. In stereoscopic viewing, different images are presented to each eye so that they unite into one three-dimensional appearance.",
